{"id": "EUVD-2026-103464", "enisaUuid": "01a7a76e-0c33-32cb-b6d4-64fe4c48fbc9", "description": "libtta through 2.3 contains an integer overflow vulnerability in tta_decoder_init_get_info() that allows attackers to cause a heap buffer overflow on 32-bit builds via unvalidated header fields. Attackers can supply a crafted .tta file with a sample rate of 1 and large samples value, wrapping the seek table allocation and crashing applications.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T11:38:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T16:01:06", "baseScore": 5.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/libtta-seek-table-count-overflow-oob-write", "https://github.com/gchudov/libtta/blob/af8dc48ce859e98842ab1a3eec98416d22a5199e/libtta.c#L602-L616", "https://github.com/gchudov/libtta/blob/af8dc48ce859e98842ab1a3eec98416d22a5199e/libtta.c#L473-L485", "https://sourceforge.net/projects/tta/", "https://github.com/gchudov/libtta", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libtta-through-2.3-integer-overflow-via-tta-decoder-init-get-info-seek-table"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112011", "GHSA-8j2j-vgj4-crmj"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f04c832e-3500-345d-a83d-55bc8c4799aa", "product": {"name": "libtta", "vendor": {"name": "True Audio"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3979b1d4-af89-37c8-978b-c6f30b08ca6e", "vendor": {"name": "True Audio"}}], "isExploited": false}